WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.440
This is The Spread, your energy
markets briefing for Friday,

2
00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:05.280
the thirtieth of October.

3
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:10.240
This episode is written with AI,
and read by an AI clone of my voice.

4
00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:14.000
France says Europe will release
forty-two million barrels of emergency

5
00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.440
oil stocks over the next three months.

6
00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:20.240
Half of it is diesel, which makes
this the most direct relief yet for

7
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:24.760
record diesel prices. Meanwhile a
tanker was left burning off Oman,

8
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:27.960
and a US approach to
Tehran pulled crude back.

9
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.840
On the markets. Brent traded at one
hundred and fourteen dollars ten

10
00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.760
on Thursday, according
to OilPrice dot com.

11
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:38.120
West Texas Intermediate was at
one hundred and one dollars fifty,

12
00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:40.360
and both were down from Wednesday.

13
00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:44.160
European gas touched one hundred
euros a megawatt hour on Wednesday,

14
00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:48.000
and EU gas storage stood at seventy-four
point nine percent full on the

15
00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:51.720
twenty-eighth of October, according
to Gas Infrastructure Europe.

16
00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:54.600
Europe's stock release comes
from France's economy minister,

17
00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:58.720
Roland Lescure. He says the forty-two
million barrels will go out over

18
00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:02.200
three months, according to
OilPrice dot com and Rigzone.

19
00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:06.120
That works out to roughly four hundred
and sixty thousand barrels a day.

20
00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:09.560
France's own share includes
ten million barrels of diesel.

21
00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:12.800
Lescure says it will start reaching
the market within days and will be

22
00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:17.200
sold at cost. He expects pump prices
to fall by twelve to eighteen cents

23
00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:19.480
a litre, possibly from next week.

24
00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:21.680
These figures come from Paris alone.

25
00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:24.880
No other government has confirmed
them, and neither has the International

26
00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:28.560
Energy Agency. It also isn't clear
whether the barrels come out of the

27
00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:31.800
agency's final one hundred
million barrel tranche.

28
00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:35.013
Country shares beyond France's
haven't been published yet.

29
00:01:35.067 --> 00:01:37.720
The diesel targets
Europe's tightest barrel.

30
00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:41.600
On Wednesday, Energy Commissioner
Dan Jorgensen called two decades of

31
00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:45.893
EU refinery closures a mistake,
with diesel at all-time highs,

32
00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:49.493
and energy ministers met on
Thursday to discuss winter prices.

33
00:01:49.547 --> 00:01:53.960
For importers, stock diesel now
competes head-on with incoming cargoes.

34
00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.800
US Gulf Coast barrels have already
been priced out of Europe by freight,

35
00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:01.280
and diesel cracks in northwest Europe
could soften as the French supply

36
00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:02.220
lands.

37
00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:06.080
Over in the Gulf, a tanker was left
burning and largely submerged after

38
00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:08.840
a suspected projectile strike off Oman.

39
00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:11.800
It happened about nine
nautical miles north of Khasab,

40
00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:16.080
on the Musandam Peninsula, according
to Nigeria's Vanguard newspaper.

41
00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:19.920
UK maritime authorities confirmed
reports of a vessel on fire off the

42
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.200
Omani coast.

43
00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:25.840
Much is still unknown. The ship's name,
its cargo and the attacker haven't

44
00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:29.600
been reported, and the
sinking itself is unconfirmed.

45
00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:33.360
This is the narrowest part of the
strait, where the US has already told

46
00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:36.000
ships to avoid unnecessary transits.

47
00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:39.040
The security worries now
reach the conference circuit.

48
00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:43.600
Reuters reported, citing sources, that
Exxon chief executive Darren Woods

49
00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:47.600
and Chevron upstream president Clay
Neff have cancelled plans to attend

50
00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:51.120
the Abu Dhabi International
Petroleum Exhibition and Conference,

51
00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:55.200
known as ADIPEC. Washington is weighing
further military action against

52
00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:56.000
Iran.

53
00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:58.160
Diplomacy is also in play.

54
00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:01.440
The Wall Street Journal reported that
Vice President Vance wrote to the

55
00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:06.000
secretary of Iran's Supreme National
Security Council to restart talks,

56
00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:08.107
and that's what pulled Brent lower.

57
00:03:08.133 --> 00:03:10.640
Tehran's response hasn't been reported.

58
00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:14.560
Later in the day, crude whipsawed on
conflicting reports about US military

59
00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:16.720
plans, according to Rigzone.

60
00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:20.480
Turning to earnings, where third-quarter
results show what record refining

61
00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:24.640
margins are worth. Shell posted
adjusted earnings of ten point eight

62
00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:27.640
billion dollars, its highest
since twenty twenty-two,

63
00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:30.280
according to OilPrice dot com and Rigzone.

64
00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:32.853
A year ago it was five point four billion,

65
00:03:32.907 --> 00:03:35.640
and Shell added a five
billion dollar buyback.

66
00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:38.600
TotalEnergies earned nine
point one billion dollars,

67
00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:41.480
up one hundred and twenty-seven
percent on the year.

68
00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:45.200
It expects liquefied natural gas
prices and refining margins to hold

69
00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:49.440
up. Phillips sixty-six reported net
profit of five point six billion

70
00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:53.200
dollars, compared with three point
nine billion in the second quarter.

71
00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:57.800
Sinopec's profit rose sixty-three point
six percent to two billion dollars.

72
00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.840
It said it couldn't fully
capture global margins.

73
00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:03.080
Consumers pay the other side of that.

74
00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:06.960
The EU has paid about eleven billion
dollars a month more for oil since

75
00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:09.680
the strait closed, according to Euronews.

76
00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:14.080
And Eurostat says the value of EU
petroleum imports rose fifty-five point

77
00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:17.880
eight percent in the second
quarter, on broadly stable volumes.

78
00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:22.480
In gas, QatarEnergy has signed a
twenty-year deal with Woodside for LNG

79
00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:25.880
from its Louisiana project,
according to Offshore Energy.

80
00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:30.320
Chief executive Saad al-Kaabi told
Reuters the company is buying long-term

81
00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:34.960
US and other supply. That way it can
still earn revenue if Hormuz exports

82
00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.320
are disrupted again.

83
00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:38.720
US exporters are benefiting too.

84
00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:42.600
Cheniere raised its full-year outlook
on demand for American cargoes,

85
00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:46.640
gCaptain reported. Kaabi's comments
didn't address this week's extension

86
00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:48.960
of Qatari force majeure to year-end.

87
00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:53.040
That extension has been reported
by buyers but not by Qatar,

88
00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:57.120
and it matters most to anyone waiting
on Qatari cargoes this winter.

89
00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:00.880
An update on the Russian
diesel tanker bound for the US.

90
00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:05.120
Ship-tracking data now shows the
Agioi Fanendes arriving at New York

91
00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:07.520
and New Jersey on the seventh of November,

92
00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:09.120
according to OilPrice dot com.

93
00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:13.600
It is carrying nearly forty thousand
tonnes of ultra-low sulphur diesel

94
00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:17.680
from Primorsk. Earlier tracking
showed it sailing "for orders",

95
00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:20.000
with Norfolk named as the destination.

96
00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:22.480
The buyer still hasn't been identified.

97
00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:27.440
In the Black Sea, the Greek-managed
boxship Contship Jet sank after three

98
00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:30.800
sea drones hit it, according
to the Bulgarian government.

99
00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:34.480
It was about seventeen nautical
miles east of Cape Kaliakra,

100
00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:36.880
sailing from Haifa to Constanta.

101
00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:40.640
Russia claims further attacks on
ships bound for Ukrainian ports,

102
00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:42.320
but those claims are unconfirmed.

103
00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:47.200
A few more things. The US Treasury's
Office of Foreign Assets Control

104
00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:51.440
amended an Iran-related general licence,
but the reports we've seen don't

105
00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:55.680
give the terms. Petrobras produced
a record of just over three and a

106
00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:59.440
half million barrels of oil
equivalent a day in the third quarter,

107
00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:04.000
according to World Oil. And offshore
shut-in figures for Hurricane Isaias

108
00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:06.160
are still pending from US regulators.

109
00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:08.400
They were due on the sixteenth of October.

110
00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:12.640
What to watch next.
Saturday, the thirty-first,

111
00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:16.320
is Senator Blumenthal's deadline
for the Agioi Fanendes owner to name

112
00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:18.000
everyone involved in the cargo.

113
00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:22.880
On Sunday, the first of November,
OPEC plus meets on December quotas.

114
00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:27.920
That is also the day Iran says it will
begin action against Sinokor tankers.

115
00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:32.000
TotalEnergies' fuel price cuts in
France take effect the same day,

116
00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:34.080
along with the French
state reserve release.

117
00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:38.320
ADIPEC runs in Abu Dhabi from the
second to the fifth of November,

118
00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:40.720
without the Exxon and Chevron executives.

119
00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:44.720
On the fourth, the EIA's weekly report
covers the week to the thirtieth

120
00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:45.840
of October.

121
00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:50.160
That's the brief. Sources for everything
you heard are in the show notes.
